WEBVTT

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.630
Sanghyuk.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.340
I brought your bag for you.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.850
You should put this on before you catch a cold.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.720
Thanks.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.310
Today I...

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.630
Thank goodness you're safe.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.890
I thought something might have happened to you.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.250
I would have brought your bag with me too,

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.440
if I'd known you were out with Yujin.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.730
Sanghyuk?

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.990
Yes, Father?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.100
You're home early; how have you been?

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.100
Hello, Mr. Kim.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.850
You must be busy with all the preparations

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.750
for your father's memorial service.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.390
Oh gosh, I totally forgot!

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.860
You'll have to excuse me, Mr. Kim.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.780
I'll see you tomorrow, Joonsang.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.320
Weren't you the one who came

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.370
to my lecture not too long ago?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.510
I apologize if I was rude that day.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.470
Is he a friend of yours?

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.980
We're classmates.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.270
So you really <i>are</i> a high school student.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.830
Could you come visit me at the university some time?

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.480
I want to talk to you about something.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.350
Yes, sir.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.030
Do you know him, Father?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.760
It looks like you have yourself a very talented friend.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.830
You should go in the house, Father; it's cold out here.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:25.870
I will.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.980
I won't do it again, I promise.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.650
You don't want Dad to be sad on a day like this, do you?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.860
So lighten up a bit, Mom.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.780
Look at you, with that hair pin on just for Dad.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.330
That's the one Dad gave you as his very first present, right?

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.660
Would you stop trying to embarrass me like that?

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.370
You always put it on for Dad's memorial services

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.690
and special occasions, though.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.350
Oh, you.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.320
What about Dad did you actually like?

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.450
Why do you ask?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.820
I'm just curious.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.540
He was gruff and didn't talk much...

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.460
He was a rather blunt man, to be honest.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.330
I wonder why I liked him so much back then.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.880
Why I wanted to see him so much and why I longed for him so...

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.150
So why did you like him, then?

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.190
There must have been a reason.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.880
It's been so long that I don't remember anymore.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.260
That makes no sense.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.100
You just don't want to tell me, do you?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.100
Do you need a reason to like someone?

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.580
Yujin, you found someone you like, didn't you?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.130
Am I right?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.900
Oh no, it's nothing like that.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.260
A round of applause, guys.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.930
You guys make such a cute couple!

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:22.650
What's all the fuss about?

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:28.990
You two over there!

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.410
Joonsang Kang!

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.150
Yujin Jung!

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:34.080
Come here.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.130
On the double!

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.810
I don't know about Joonsang,

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.420
but I never expected <i>you</i> to cut class, Yujin,

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.650
despite being late all the time.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.650
You two are now in charge of cleaning the toilets and the incinerator

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.610
until winter break.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.610
And be nice to each other while you do it, okay?

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:09.820
Where's your answer?

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:10.640
Yes, sir.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.500
Hey, Yujin.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.210
Did Joonsang threaten you?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.290
What?

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.630
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.420
What are you going to do—

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.130
I said Joonsang was mine, didn't I?

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.470
You did. Why?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.820
Yet you dared to make a move on him.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.140
Make a move?

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.850
What are you talking about?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.690
Yujin only went with him because she was threatened—

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:41.900
Shut up when adults are talking, kid.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.770
Who are you calling a kid?

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.360
I guess they're right when they say ugly girls travel in groups.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.450
You're one to talk, when you drown your face in make-up everyday.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.410
You better watch your mouth!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.200
This is my pure, natural face, right here.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.180
You're not fooling anyone

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.720
with those double-eyelids you make every morning.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.800
Is there anything better than the smell of burning leaves?

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.170
It smells like roasting coffee beans.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.720
Almost like ripe hazelnut.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:19.020
I take the rake in my hand and I keep...

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.180
What are you doing?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.900
I know what coffee smells like, but I don't know what hazelnut smells like.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.440
I thought maybe I could find out if I smelled them.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.070
I think it smells like Dad though.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:35.700
Like, whenever I caught him secretly smoking

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.060
he'd hug me and say,

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.160
"If you keep it a secret from Mom, I'll buy you ice cream."

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.210
That's what they smelled like.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:56.100
Are you the type of person who never repeats a mistake?

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.120
Or are you the type of person who tells herself that she won't,

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:00.930
but does it anyway?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.100
What are you talking about?

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.130
If you were to decide never to see someone again,

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.780
could you actually keep to it even if you wanted to see that person?

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:11.900
Or would you...

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.030
Of course you have to.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:15.950
I mean,

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.700
I'd go see that person, if it were me.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.450
Why?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.410
Do you need a reason for wanting to see someone?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.040
I thought I'd seen you somewhere before,

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.220
but I never guessed you were Sanghyuk's friend.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.970
Here, have a cup.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.500
It may taste a little bitter at first,

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.400
but you'll like it once you get used to it.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.310
Why don't I cut to the chase;

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.900
would you like to study with me?

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.400
Why are you interested in me?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.160
Well, believe it or not,

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:02.470
I've never met anyone quite like you in my twenty years of teaching.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.790
Don't get the wrong impression;

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.840
I'm not saying I'm just going to unconditionally teach you.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.630
Oh, this picture?

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.760
It's from when we went to Lake Eui'am not too long ago.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.050
How's my Sanghyuk when he's at school?

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.640
We're not very good friends.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:25.810
That Sanghyuk...

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.110
He may not be as talented as you are,

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.310
but he's a really nice kid.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.820
You must love him very much.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.820
Of course I do; he's my only son.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.570
What kind of a father doesn't love his son?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.330
I'm sure your father feels the same way.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:00.010
This is that song you played for me, isn't it?

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.390
It was called...

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.140
Oh yeah, "The First Time", right?

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.810
"The First Time"...

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.060
You can have it, if you want.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:14.530
Oh no, I like it better when <i>you</i> play it for me.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.830
Do you want to go see a movie with me on Saturday?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.210
I've never asked someone this before.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:48.930
Anyone can just simply copy the shape of someone's facial features;

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.440
as I explained at the beginning of the lecture,

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:51.690
Hey, Sanghyuk!

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:54.630
a self-portrait is supposed to depict internal features

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:55.730
that only you can see inside yourself,

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:58.860
and bring them to life through an objet d'art.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.490
Not bad.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:02.490
Hey, Jinsook!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:07.720
Send it over that way.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.810
Ten more minutes.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.560
I think drawing something that's a reflection of yourself

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.030
is much better experience than drawing a vase or a bust.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:40.990
Could you explain your picture?

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:42.110
Oh, I...

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.530
Stand up and explain it to the whole class, please.

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.910
I guess you can't really call it a self-portrait,

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.380
but should I say that it's a wish of mine?

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:53.790
I want to become somebody's house.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.580
Could I ask you why?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.050
My father once told me,

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:02.220
"A loving heart is the best home that two loving people could have."

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.600
The rooms may not be big, and the roof may be crooked,

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.540
but I want to become a house that someone can always come home to

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:10.810
and rest.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.770
We've finally agreed on a date, Yujin!

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.570
A date for what?

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.570
This Saturday's Christmas, right?

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:26.820
We decided that the Radio Club is going to go camping at Chelin's cabin.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:27.970
You're coming, aren't you?

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.580
Of course she is.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.350
We only have five members;

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.040
it wouldn't be the same if even one didn't go.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.370
We have six, remember?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.880
I don't think I can go.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:40.590
Why?

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.380
Come on, why can't you go?

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.350
I already have plans for that day, so I can't.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.390
Is it something important?

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:53.180
Sorry.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.560
You have to go, Yujin!

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:56.640
Oh come on, Yujin!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:56.650
Hey, it's Joonsang.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.020
We're going to go on a Radio Club camping trip, Joonsang.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.190
We're going on Saturday;

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.150
you can make it, right?

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.570
Sorry, I already have plans.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.250
Joonsang has something on Saturday, too?

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.510
It won't be any fun without Yujin;

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:17.000
if she's not going, I'm not either.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.340
dx = h.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.800
Since dy = k, that means z = y will have to be...

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:29.180
What if f(x) was a primitive function within this interval?

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:33.180
Why don't we just partially differentiate here?

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.640
That's an interesting idea.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.870
Why don't you try solving it?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:39.860
You want me to do it?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.690
This is the first time I've seen you smile.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.610
You should smile more; it suits you well.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.190
Who could it be?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.220
Who is it?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.220
What brings you here at this hour, Sanghyuk?

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.680
Come in.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.060
No, I'll just say it here.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.230
Come camping with us on Saturday.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.190
I told you I had plans.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:24.150
Listen to me just this once.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.240
I don't understand why you're doing this.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:30.240
You're meeting up with Joonsang, aren't you?

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:40.750
I don't care if you like Joonsang or someone else,

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.380
but I just can't bear to see you get hurt.

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.250
He's not that kind of guy.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.760
I think you two are alike.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.950
You're so alike that you push yourselves away from each other,

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.800
kind of like two similar magnetic poles.

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:57.100
You already know him so well, don't you?

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.770
I know <i>you</i> well, Sanghyuk.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.480
You're just not good at expressing it.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:06.570
What?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:10.530
You're not the kind of guy who usually hates another person.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:12.780
He's...

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:13.870
That's enough.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.240
Sanghyuk...

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.800
No extracurricular lessons for you today?

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.590
What are you talking about?

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.110
I saw you with my father.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.940
Why did you go to my father?

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.570
I just wanted to find out what kind of person he was.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:52.070
You do realize that what you said made no sense, right?

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:56.030
Why exactly are you doing this to me?

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:58.370
You have too much.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:15:59.720
What?

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:03.500
Whenever I see someone who has everything, like you,

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.080
I just want to take it away from them.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.550
And that's why you got close to Yujin?

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.440
To steal something from me?

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.380
You bastard.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.650
If you had a problem, you should have taken it up with me.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.780
Why did you have to involve Yujin?

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:20.350
You did everything just to rub it in my face

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:23.270
when you don't even like her, didn't you?

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:26.330
Come on, answer me.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:27.690
Answer me!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:28.520
That's right.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.860
You bastard!

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:41.870
Yujin...

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.960
Did you mean what you just said?

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.650
Did you?

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:58.390
Yujin...

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:03.680
I don't think I can go out with you this Saturday, Joonsang.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.980
Sorry, I forgot I had other plans already.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.410
Hurry up will you? You're driving me crazy.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.710
Okay, okay, I was just buying corn dogs.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:29.270
We're going to be late. Let's board.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.840
Joonsang's not here yet.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.340
Shouldn't we hurry up?

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.930
Over here, Joonsang!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:39.930
He's really here.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.780
I told you he would come.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.730
Put an end to this whole thing, Sanghyuk; I'll help you.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.160
What took you so long?

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:49.650
We were all waiting.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.570
Come on guys, the train's about to leave.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:00.410
Why is Yujin giving Joonsang the cold shoulder?

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.410
Hurry up!

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:05.290
Something happened between those two, didn't it?

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:06.430
I wouldn't know.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:07.430
Let me guess,

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.650
Yujin got dumped, and now she's trying to ignore him.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.380
I guess you could call it a hurt woman's last remaining shred of dignity.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.690
We're almost there.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:18.800
There it is.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.450
This place is awesome!

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:26.020
Hey, Joonsang.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.440
Look at those two.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.190
They're really funny.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.550
They say that they're only childhood friends,

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.980
but that's just a naïve excuse, don't you think?

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:36.960
An excuse?

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:38.990
You were right to dump Yujin.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.410
Just let her have fun with Sanghyuk.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.300
I bet you like how honest I am;

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.290
I'm not dishonest like she is.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.540
You like me, don't you?

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:52.920
I bet you joined the radio club because I was in it, didn't you?

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.130
Okay, I'll go out with you.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:56.980
You're really funny.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:01.510
Too bad your imagination is wasted on writing romance novels like that.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.700
The air out here is really nice, isn't it?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:09.610
Yeah.

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.140
Now that I think about it,

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:15.270
we made tteokbokki this time last year too, didn't we?

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:19.190
You and Huijin ruined it by putting in too much hot chili paste.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.610
But it should be okay this time.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.200
Wow, it's hot!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.150
Do we have any fish cakes?

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:28.040
You can't have tteokbokki without fish cakes.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.040
This is no good.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:30.910
My tongue is all burnt!

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:31.790
Are you okay?

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.440
Why is this thing so long?

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:39.050
We have to set up that part too?

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:41.400
Hoist it up already.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:42.950
That takes <i>effort</i> though.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.120
Would you quit whining and just do it already?

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.120
I wasn't whining!

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.380
I'm just saying it's good the way it is now.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.230
I'm going to turn it on, okay?

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:53.100
Go for it.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.360
Here it comes...

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:56.570
Tada!

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:07.990
Why don't we make up a story by telling parts of it in turns?

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.580
Sounds fun, let's do it.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.580
I'll go first.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.390
Once upon a time,

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.540
there were a man and a woman named Cheolsoo and Yeonghee.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.560
Could you get any more stereotypical?

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:19.590
You're into this too much.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:22.550
Yeah, couldn't you do better than "Cheolsoo and Yeonghee"?

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.590
Who cares.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.340
You're next, Sanghyuk.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:30.850
The two had been good friends since they were little.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:34.160
But one day, a wonderful man named Minsoo

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.520
confessed his love to Yeonghee,

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.590
since she was so beautiful.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.820
In your dreams.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:43.590
You want to die?

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.200
Okay, okay.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:49.620
Yeonghee didn't know who to choose: Cheolsoo or Minsoo.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.830
Their relationship slowly turned into a love triangle.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:52.540
This is good, right?

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:53.620
Yeah.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.830
It's your turn, Yujin.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:20:59.630
Come on.

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:07.030
Yeonghee found out that everything Minsoo had told her was a lie.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.310
You're the last one, Joonsang.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:19.310
In the end, Minsoo said to Yeonghee:

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.670
"I'm sorry."

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:30.410
Yujin.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:33.790
What I said back then was a mistake.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.180
A mistake?

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:37.080
Exactly what part of it was a mistake?

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.170
Was it a mistake that you used me to get at Sanghyuk?

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.190
See?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.650
You can't say anything.

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.110
And there I was, all happy,

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:49.890
without a single clue as to what was going on.

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:52.390
Was it fun for you?

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:54.520
I was serious about everything.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:57.480
You need to be careful when you use the word "serious" like that.

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:00.860
I don't want to make excuses;

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:02.290
it was my fault.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.900
But shouldn't you at least hear my side of the story?

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.780
You shouldn't just one-sidedly believe everything Sanghyuk—

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:09.140
All right then, tell me.

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:10.910
Is there more that I don't know about?

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:12.950
You sure have a lot of secrets.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:15.910
What's with that tone of voice, Yujin?

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:17.790
I've got nothing more to say to you,

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:19.500
and I don't want to hear anything from you either.

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:24.480
You're right.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:27.300
Everything I said, and the promise I made to you {i don't remember if he makes more than one promise}

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:29.470
was all a lie.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:32.220
Satisfied?

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:38.480
Yujin!

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:52.450
Where am I?

00:22:57.620 --> 00:22:58.680
Did you find her?

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:01.420
I looked everywhere around back, but she wasn't there.

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:02.580
She's not on the second floor either.

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:04.340
Hey, where's Joonsang?

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:07.050
What? They disappeared together?

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:07.960
Hey, Joonsang...

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:09.260
Have you seen Yujin?

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:10.400
Where's Yujin?

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:11.860
Joonsang.

00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:16.350
Oh no, Yujin...

00:23:16.970 --> 00:23:17.850
Yujin!

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:19.980
Yujin, where are you?

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:21.290
Yujin!

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:23.900
Yujin!

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:27.980
Yujin!

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:31.200
Say something if you can hear my voice, Yujin.

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:32.660
Yujin!
